# Multi-Agent Delegation Kit — Project-Level Configuration
# Path: <project_root>/.agents/delegation/config.env
# Priority: CLI flags > Project config (this file) > User config > Kit defaults
#
# Notes:
# - Safe KEY=VALUE format only (parsed without shell eval for repo safety).
# - Override only project-specific settings here (e.g. test command, budget, role overrides).

# --- Project test, eval & safe local Git defaults ---
# DELEGATE_DEFAULT_TEST_CMD is the command prefix list a delegated Claude Code may run unattended
# (each comma-separated prefix becomes a Bash(<prefix>:*) rule), so name the narrowest prefixes
# that cover this repo's checks and routine Git wrap-up:
#   pytest                       -> pytest tests/...
#   npm test,npm run,node --test -> Node.js test/eval scripts without npm install / npm exec
#   go test,go vet               -> go test ./..., go vet ./...
#
# Recommended Node.js template (full tests/evals + routine local Git wrap-up via coder):
# DELEGATE_DEFAULT_TEST_CMD=npm test,npm run,node --test,git status,git diff,git log,git add,git commit
#
# Optional: append `,git push` ONLY when you want coder to push after explicit user approval.
# Safety red lines (enforce in briefs & rules):
#   - NEVER run `git push` without explicit user authorization in the current turn.
#   - NEVER use destructive flags (`--force`, `git reset --hard`, `git clean -fd`).
#   - NEVER use `git add -A` or `git add .` (always stage explicit allowlisted file paths).
# Without DELEGATE_DEFAULT_TEST_CMD, the kit default (python3) applies.
# DELEGATE_DEFAULT_FALLBACK=fast            # comma-separated chain is allowed, e.g. fast,scout
# DELEGATE_DEFAULT_EFFORT=high
# DELEGATE_DEFAULT_MAX_BUDGET=1.00          # none or 0 removes the cap
# DELEGATE_DEFAULT_TIMEOUT=300s

# --- Optional project-specific role override ---
# DELEGATE_ROLE_CODER=claude:sonnet
# DELEGATE_DISABLED_HARNESSES=
# DELEGATE_DISABLED_PRESETS=
# DELEGATE_INHERIT_SUBAGENT=deny            # in this repo, refuse native `self` workers so coding goes to the coder channel
